with almost 500 sessions next 2019 it's  understandable that you can get to all  of them so if you didn't see cloud data  fusion data integration at Google cloud  then stay tuned because here is the  rewind the biggest barrier to enterprise  data analysis and machine learning is  data integration it is not uncommon to  see companies struggle to get their data  in one place move it around transform it  and make sense out of it because  honestly it's really hard problem to  solve cloud data fusion is a fully  managed cloud native data integration  service that helps users efficiently  build and manage data pipelines with the  graphical interface and a broad  open-source library of pre-configured  connectors and transformations data  fusion shifts and organizations focus  away from code and integration to  insights and action data Fusion is built  on the open source project seed app and  this open core ensures data pipeline  portability for users data fusion aims  at making the lives of data  practitioners easier by providing a  graphical user interface to visually  drag-and-drop elements to create data  pipelines and then finally run it on GCP  in data fusion we collect metadata  information on fields and tables and  expose them as lineage so you can do  root cause analysis and impact analysis  data fusion can solve a variety of use  cases if you are building a data  warehouse using bigquery you should look  at data fusion since it can connect to  multiple different data sources like  Oracle and other relational and  non-relational databases if you're  looking to retire a legacy system data  fusion can help you migrate the data to  GCP if you're looking to consolidate  data or in a hybrid environment you can  use data fusion for data consistency  across cloud and on-premise in  data fusion natively integrates with  Google cloud which simplifies data  security and ensures your data is  immediately available for analysis data  fusion offers both pre-configured  transformations from an OSS library as  well as the ability to create an  internal library of custom connections  and transformations that can be  validated shared and reused across an  organization it lays the foundation of  collaborative data engineering and  improves productivity this means less  waiting for data engineers and  importantly less sweating about code  quality if you'd like to see the full  talk and the demo check out the link in  the description below and don't forget  to subscribe to the cloud YouTube  channel for more great next rewind  content thank you for watching  [Music]
 

